        "content": "## What this does not measure\n\n- **Message content.** No console line, exception value or event attribute carries a message body, and nothing here reads one.\n- **DIDs.** The user id is a salted hash, never the DID. `page_url` is Faro session metadata rather than an event attribute and does carry the space DID and room id in its path, which is why *Top routes* shows them.\n- **Tile views are counted per session, not per render.** A `tile_view` is reported once a session per tile, so a room that re-renders its timeline does not inflate the count — and a user who scrolls back past the same tile is not counted twice. `tile_error` is empty while nothing fails to load, and an empty panel is not a broken query.\n- **Native (Tauri) builds.** They emit nothing to this stack as of today; every panel undercounts desktop usage.\n- **Who is anonymous.** An empty `user_id` is not distinguishable from a build without the salt, and neither can be recovered after the fact.\n- **Server-side behaviour.** Everything here is browser telemetry; appserver request rates and latency live in the appserver metrics and traces, not in this dashboard.",
